ut one share the same size. The output is the square whose size appears only once. Checked against these lists, the rule picks the correct crop in all four pairs.\n\n**Test input.** The square sizes are 23, 23, 23, 23 and **21**. The 21-cell square has bounding box rows 7–11, columns 0–4 and is the answer. Its checkerboard of holes is the same pattern as pair 2's output.\n\n**Construction stages.**\n1. Find the square objects.\n2. Count how often each size occurs.\n3. Pick the square with the unique size.\n4. Crop its bounding box and emit that crop as the result.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    from collections import Counter\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    objs = objects(g, bg=bg)\n    cnt = Counter(o[\"size\"] for o in objs)\n    # odd one out: object whose size is unique; fallback to the smallest\n    uniq = [o for o in objs if cnt[o[\"size\"]] == 1]\n    chosen = uniq[0] if uniq else min(objs, key=lambda o: o[\"size\"])\n    y0, x0, y1, x1 = chosen[\"box\"]\n    out = crop(g, y0, x0, y1, x1)\n    emit(out, f\"Crop the square whose cell count ({chosen['size']}) occurs only once among all squares.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"In pair 3 the chosen square has only one hole and is the largest object (24 cells)."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"In every pair, all squares but one share the same size."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Pick the square with the unique size."}],"topology":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each square has a few black \"holes\" punched into it."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Which square is chosen.** It is not always the one with the most holes."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"In pair 3 the chosen square has only one hole and is the largest object (24 cells)."}],"count":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"What the chosen squares have in common is that each is the odd one out by cell count:"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Count how often each size occurs."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Crop the square whose cell count (22) occurs only once among all squares."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Every output is exactly one of those squares, cropped from the input; the fact sheet confirms that each output is an exact crop."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Checked against these lists, the rule picks the correct crop in all four pairs."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"The 21-cell square has bounding box rows 7–11, columns 0–4 and is the answer."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"e8b7204bdc72b0ebdf210a4e9b281b1f4d2b3d7ecfdb9823cd1b4da297d5f955","task_sha256":"754d70342c71339d981e2390227eaa8fd4a767cf521ea6a8f1040773935262e2","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
